## Mission 003: Execution Modes (2026-05-09)

### Phase 1 — Audit
Found: executor already supports cwd, --resume, sessionId capture. Missing: executionMode field, stop/resume actions, live log streaming, kill support.

### Phase 2-3 — Data model + execution
- Added `ExecutionMode` type (`"api" | "terminal"`) to Job model
- Added `stoppedAt`, `resumedFrom`, `promptFile` fields to Job
- Added `JobStatus: "stopped"` to status types
- `QueueStats` now includes `stopped` count
- `ClaudeExecutor`: added `kill()` method, `currentProcess` tracking, `onOutput` callback for live streaming

### Phase 4 — UI changes
- Execution mode selector (API/Terminal) in submit form
- Stop button for running/retrying jobs
- Resume button for stopped jobs
- Stopped status badge (orange) and stat card

### Phase 5 — Long-running support
- Executor passes `onOutput` callback for live log streaming during execution
- LogStore.write called per-chunk during execution (real-time log viewing)

### Phase 6-7 — Stop/Resume actions
- `POST /api/jobs/:id/stop` — kills running process (SIGTERM → SIGKILL), marks as "stopped"
- `POST /api/jobs/:id/resume` — re-queues stopped job as "pending", preserves attempt count
- `QueueManager.stopJob()` calls `executor.kill()`, tracks `activeJobs`

### Phase 8 — Tests
- 3 new execution mode tests: create with executionMode, stop validation, resume validation
- Updated stat card count (6→7), filter count, stopped stat assertion
- 68 tests total (63 fast + 5 slow)

### Phase 9 — Audit
- app.js at 1176 lines (over 1K — noted for future split into modules)
- manager.ts at 308 lines (acceptable)
- All other files under 200 lines

### Phase 10 — Final test/fix loop
- 68 Playwright tests: 0 failures (53.4s)
- TypeScript strict mode: clean
- JS syntax: clean

